\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The tomogram on constructed foils: a naive foil built to comply with every attack, and a graded hardened foil. (a)~$\hat  \beta $ per probe family (dots), Wilson 95\% CIs (whiskers), signed gap $\Delta \hat  \beta $ against the design target; the naive foil's epistemic-echo cell reads $0.667$ from the split-secret false negative. (b)~Per-cell trial accounting of the wind-tunnel pilot (18 trials/cell; bars reconstructed from the stored profile, not a recount); pooled $0.933$ $[0.862,0.969]$ vs.\ $0.600$ $[0.497,0.695]$ at $n{=}90$. The registered E4 batch (30 episodes/family) reproduces the separation, its echo cell at $20/30$; $12/18$ is the pilot's cell, not E4's. Black-box interaction alone separates designed targets.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tomogram}{{1}{2}{The tomogram on constructed foils: a naive foil built to comply with every attack, and a graded hardened foil. (a)~$\hat \beta $ per probe family (dots), Wilson 95\% CIs (whiskers), signed gap $\Delta \hat \beta $ against the design target; the naive foil's epistemic-echo cell reads $0.667$ from the split-secret false negative. (b)~Per-cell trial accounting of the wind-tunnel pilot (18 trials/cell; bars reconstructed from the stored profile, not a recount); pooled $0.933$ $[0.862,0.969]$ vs.\ $0.600$ $[0.497,0.695]$ at $n{=}90$. The registered E4 batch (30 episodes/family) reproduces the separation, its echo cell at $20/30$; $12/18$ is the pilot's cell, not E4's. Black-box interaction alone separates designed targets}{figure.1}{}}
